class.description:
A [LocalizationCatalog] is a table: one row per key (a key and an optional context) and one column per locale. [TextLocalizationCatalog] stores texts, [ResourceLocalizationCatalog] stores localized resource paths. Rows are addressed by key and context, or by their row number (see [method find_key]). The data is stored compactly: every locale is one column of UTF-8 text with one 4-byte offset per row, so a message costs its text plus 4 bytes (instead of an interned [StringName] per message like in [Translation]). [b]Files:[/b] [method load_from_file] and [method save_to_file] choose the format by the file extension. The binary [code].lcat[/code] format stores one block per locale: a catalog loaded from it (also with [method @GDScript.load]) reads only the keys and the locale table; the text of a locale is read when it is first used, or with [method load_locale]. This keeps unused locales out of memory and works from the PCK and [code]user://[/code] on every platform, including the Web. [b]Text formats[/b] ([method load_from_text], [method to_text], [enum ResourceTextSerializer.Format]): - CSV: the layout of Godot's CSV translation importer. Column 0 holds the keys, every other column a locale. A [code]?context[/code] column holds the context, a [code]?plural[/code] column the plural key (text catalogs) and starts plural rows, a [code]?type[/code] column holds the expected type (resource catalogs). Columns starting with [code]_[/code] are ignored, a row starting with [code]?pluralrule[/code] holds the plural rule per locale. Translations are unescaped with [method String.c_unescape], keys are not. - JSON, YAML, TOML, INI: one entry per key, [code]key: {locale: text}[/code]; plural forms are an array. Fields starting with [code]_[/code] are not locales: [code]_context[/code], [code]_key[/code] (the key, when the entry name differs from it, as for [code]"BACK@menu"[/code]), [code]_plural[/code] (text catalogs) or [code]_type[/code] (resource catalogs). The entry [code]?catalog[/code] holds [code skip-lint]locales[/code] (their order) and [code]plural_rules[/code]. In INI, every key is a [code][section][/code]. - XML: [code]<catalog locales="en,de"><message key="HELLO" context="menu"><text locale="de">Hallo</text></message></catalog>[/code], one [code]<text>[/code] per plural form, [code]<plural_rule locale="de">[/code] elements for the plural rules. Saved as [code].tres[/code] or [code].res[/code], a catalog stores all locales in one block (no loading per locale). [codeblocks] [gdscript] var catalog = TextLocalizationCatalog.new() catalog.load_from_file("res://translations/ui.csv") catalog.save_to_file("user://ui.lcat")
var lazy = load("user://ui.lcat") as TextLocalizationCatalog print(lazy.is_locale_loaded("de")) # false print(lazy.get_text("HELLO", "de")) # Loads "de" only. [/gdscript] [csharp] var catalog = new TextLocalizationCatalog(); catalog.LoadFromFile("res://translations/ui.csv"); catalog.SaveToFile("user://ui.lcat");
var lazy = GD.Load<TextLocalizationCatalog>("user://ui.lcat"); GD.Print(lazy.IsLocaleLoaded("de")); // false GD.Print(lazy.GetText("HELLO", "de")); // Loads "de" only. [/csharp] [/codeblocks] [b]Note:[/b] [code].csv[/code] files in a project are imported by the CSV translation importer. To read them at runtime with [method load_from_file], set their import mode to "Keep File (exported as is)", or convert them to [code].lcat[/code]. [b]Note:[/b] Reading the same catalog from several threads is safe (loading a locale is guarded by a lock); changing it while other threads read it is not.
